  "source_dataset": "CADECV2",
  "text": "Leg cramps, back muscle injury from low magnisium caused by Nexium.\nI have been using Miralax and psillium every night for about a year and wanted to try Linzess, but my doctor was hesitant to let me try it.\nPossible side effects.\nAnyway, after some reasearch, I realized the Nexium I have been using causes a Magnesium deficiency.\nSo now I take a multi-mineral capsule and a 500mg Magnesium capsule 3 times a day with meals.\nI have been able to cut back on my chemical medications and have some hope that I will be able to get off them completely by adjusting my mineral intake.\nTry this, because your boweles can not function without enough minerals.\n",
